<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Notes   n1. Current tax include tax pertaining to earlier period / year:  n                                                                             Quarter                         Nine Months   n                  n               Current Tax                                               =     562                                     592          n               Tax pertaining to earlier period / year       =  (128)                                   (124)  n  n2. Total profit or loss attributable to, include :                         Quarter                     Nine Months   n                Net Profit attributabl to :  n                            Owners of the parent                                            2253                                1944   n                            Non controlling interest                                           75                                      97  n             Other comprehensible income attributabl to :  n                            Owners of the parent                                             82                                      496  n                            Non controlling interest                                            0                                         0  n  nNotes :  n  n1. The above standalone results were reviewed by the Audit Committee and then approved by the Board of Directors at their respective meetings held on 07 February 2021.  n2. The Statement has been prepared in accordance with the Ind AS notified under Companies (Ind AS) Rules, 2015 prescribed under section 133 of the Companies Act, 2013 read with rule 3 of the Companies (Indian Accounting Standards) Rules, 2015 (as amended).  n3. Current tax for the quarter ended 31 December 2019 is net of credit arising during the said quarter, against expected current tax provisions recognised in the earlier quarters of the respective years.  n4. Trade receivables outstanding as at 31 December 2020 include Rs. 2,633 lakhs, outstanding from customers situated outside India. There are delays in receipt of remittance pending settlement beyond the timeline stipulated by the FED Master Direction No. 16/2015-16, under the Foreign Exchange Management Act, 1999. The Company is in the process of recovering these outstanding dues, however provision wherever required has been made in the books.  Further, Company is in the process of regularising these delays by filing necessary applications with the appropriate authority for condonation of delays / penalties, if any. Pending conclusion of the aforesaid matter, the amount of penalty, if any, that may be levied, is not ascertainable..  n5. The spread of COVID-19 had impacted the businesses from middle of the month of March 2020. The Company has considered the possible effects that may result from the pandemic relating to COVID-19 on the carrying values of its property, plant and equipment, investment, inventories and receivables and carried out a detailed assessment of its liquidity position for the next one year including recoverability of carrying value of its assets. In developing the assumptions, the Company has considered internal and certain external sources of information including reliable credit reports, economic forecasts and industry reports up to the date of approval of the interim standalone financial results and expects to recover the carrying amount of its assets.   n6. Operating segments are reported in a manner consistent with the integral reporting provided to the Chief Operating Decision Maker (CODM). The CODM regularly monitors and reviews the operating result of the whole Company as one segment  Bearing . Thus, as defined under Ind AS 108  Operating Segments , the Company's entire business falls under one operational segment.</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
